25. Queue Complexity

For a properly implemented standard Queue:

Operation	Complexity
Enqueue	O(1)
Dequeue	O(1)
Front/Peek	O(1)
Rear/Back	O(1)
IsEmpty	O(1)
Size	O(1)

Space complexity:

O(n)

where n is the number of elements.

26. Why Queue Operations Can Become O(n)

A poorly designed array queue might shift every element after deletion:

[10][20][30][40]

Remove 10:

[20][30][40]

If every element is shifted, deletion takes:

O(n)

A better implementation moves the front index/pointer instead of shifting elements, making deletion:

O(1)

This is an important implementation detail.

27. Queue ADT

Queue can also be understood as an Abstract Data Type (ADT).

The ADT describes what operations are available, rather than exactly how they are implemented.

A Queue ADT supports operations such as:

Enqueue
Dequeue
Peek/Front
Rear/Back
IsEmpty
Size

It can then be implemented using:

Array
Linked List
Deque

and other structures.
